		<unit label="title" identifier="19.2" level="1">Criminal Procedure</unit>
		<unit label="chapter" identifier="17" level="2">Convictions; Effect Thereof</unit>
		<unit label="article" identifier="1" level="3">Proof and Verdicts</unit>
	</structure>
	<section_number>19.2-289</section_number>
	<catch_line>Conviction of petit larceny</catch_line>
	<text>
		In a prosecution for grand larceny, if it be found that the thing stolen is of less value than $1,000, the jury may find the accused guilty of petit larceny.
	</text>
	<history>Code 1950, § 19.1-252; 1960, c. 366; 1966, c. 247; 1975, c. 495; 1981, c. 197; 2018, cc. 764, 765; 2020, cc. 89, 401.</history>
</law>
